# GSP355: Create and Manage Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL Instances - Challenge Lab Guide

## Automated Environment Setup
Copy and paste this entire block directly into your **Cloud Shell Terminal**. It automatically queries your active GCP project to dynamically set your region, zone, project ID, and lab username.

```bash
# Auto-detect Zone and Region from postgres-vm
export ZONE=$(gcloud compute instances list --filter="name=postgres-vm" --format="value(zone)")
export REGION=${ZONE%-*}

# Auto-detect Project ID and Student Username
export PROJECT_ID=$(gcloud config get-value project)
export DB_USER=$(gcloud config get-value account)

# Lab specific resource names
export DB_NAME="orders"
export MIGRATION_JOB="orders-migration"
export CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE="postgres-orders"

# Set regional and zonal defaults to prevent empty parameter flags
gcloud config set compute/region $REGION
gcloud config set compute/zone $ZONE

# Verify discovered variables
echo "========================================"
echo "REGION:             $REGION"
echo "ZONE:               $ZONE"
echo "PROJECT_ID:         $PROJECT_ID"
echo "DB_USER:            $DB_USER"
echo "CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE: $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE"
echo "========================================"
Task 1: Migrate Standalone PostgreSQL to Cloud SQL
1. Configure the Source VM (postgres-vm)
SSH into postgres-vm and add the missing primary key required by PostgreSQL logical replication (pglogical):

Bash
gcloud compute ssh postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE
Inside postgres-vm, execute:

Bash
# Add missing primary key to the distribution_centers table
sudo -u postgres psql -d orders -c "ALTER TABLE distribution_centers ADD PRIMARY KEY (id);"

# Ensure the pglogical extension is created
sudo -u postgres psql -d orders -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pglogical;"

# Exit the VM back to Cloud Shell
exit
2. Create Connection Profile & Run Continuous Migration Job
Run in Cloud Shell:

Bash
# Get internal IP of postgres-vm
VM_INTERNAL_IP=$(gcloud compute instances describe postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE --format='get(networkInterfaces[0].networkIP)')

# Create source connection profile
gcloud database-migration connection-profiles create postgresql postgres-vm-profile \
    --region=$REGION \
    --host=$VM_INTERNAL_IP \
    --port=5432 \
    --username=postgres \
    --password="supersecret!" \
    --provider=POSTGRESQL

# Create continuous migration job
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs create $MIGRATION_JOB \
    --region=$REGION \
    --source=postgres-vm-profile \
    --destination-instance-id=$CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --type=CONTINUOUS \
    --connectivity-vpc=default

# Start migration job
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs start $MIGRATION_JOB --region=$REGION
Task 2: Promote Cloud SQL to a Stand-Alone Instance
1. Monitor Migration Progress
Run this command to monitor the continuous replication sync status without parameter drop errors:

Bash
watch -n 5 "gcloud database-migration migration-jobs describe $MIGRATION_JOB --region=\$(gcloud config get-value compute/region) --format='table(state,phase)'"
(Press Ctrl + C once the table shows STATE: RUNNING and PHASE: CDC or change-data-capture).

2. Promote to Standalone Instance
Execute the promotion directly from the CLI:

Bash
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs promote $MIGRATION_JOB \
    --region=$REGION \
    --quiet
Wait 2–3 minutes for Cloud SQL to detach from the source and finalize standalone restart.

Task 3: Secure the Database Using IAM DB Authentication
Enable IAM DB Authentication on the Cloud SQL instance:

Bash
gcloud sql instances patch $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --database-flags=cloudsql.iam_authentication=on
Authorize postgres-vm's external IP to connect to Cloud SQL:

Bash
VM_EXT_IP=$(gcloud compute instances describe postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE --format='get(networkInterfaces[0].accessConfigs[0].natIP)')

gcloud sql instances patch $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --authorized-networks=$VM_EXT_IP
Create the Cloud IAM database user:

Bash
gcloud sql users create $DB_USER \
    --instance=$CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --type=CLOUD_IAM_USER
Grant SELECT permissions inside the PostgreSQL database:

Bash
gcloud sql connect $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE --user=postgres --quiet
(When prompted for password, enter: supersecret!)

SQL
\c orders;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO "$DB_USER";
\q
Task 4: Configure Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR) & Storage
Enable automated backups and Point-in-Time Recovery:

Bash
gcloud sql instances patch $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --enable-point-in-time-recovery \
    --enable-bin-log
Create a clone instance if required by the lab checkpoint:

Bash
gcloud sql instances clone $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE${CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE}-pitr
